  "body": "## Problem\n\nAcross the catalogue, search and list tools returned part of a result as if it were the whole of it. A caller had no way to tell a complete answer from the first page of a larger one. The cuts took three forms:\n\n- **A fixed page with nothing said.** Results stopped at the first upstream page or at a hard-coded slice (`[:50]`, `[:200]`, `[:500]`), with no total and no way to ask for the rest.\n- **Paging arguments ignored.** `limit`/`offset`/`page` were accepted but never forwarded, or were forwarded under a name the upstream ignores.\n- **Out-of-range values sent upstream.** The upstream answered HTTP 400, and the tool reported that as a failed call instead of naming the bad argument.\n\nThis came out of the silent-failure rounds in August; #496 (round 23) was the first slice of it. The rest was never pushed. This PR ports it onto current main.\n\n## Fix\n\nAbout 300 tools now share one contract:\n\n- **Local validation.** `limit`/`offset`/`page`/`cursor` are checked before any request. A bad value returns an error that names the `parameter`.\n- **Completeness metadata** returned next to the data:\n  - `returned`\n  - `total_results` and `total_results_is_exact`\n  - `has_more`\n  - `next_offset` / `next_page` / `next_cursor`\n  - `truncated`\n  - `result_set_complete`\n  - `pagination_scope` (when the paging is local rather than upstream)\n- **Fixed caps removed** where the upstream can page. Where it cannot, the cut is disclosed instead.\n- **Main's count convention is kept** wherever main already had one (#628): `*_count` is what the page holds and `total_*` is the full figure. Snapshot tests that assumed otherwise were adapted.\n\n## Where main had moved on, main's version is kept\n\n| Tool family | What main did | What happens here |\n|---|---|---|\n| GtoPdb | Moved to bulk CSV downloads | REST-based changes dropped; paging added on top of the CSV path |\n| WormBase | Moved to the Alliance API | All snapshot changes dropped |\n| SAbDab 2 | #701 found no usable search route | Main kept, plus an unknown-parameter guard (see below) |\n| GWAS Catalog | Moved to v2 | `start` is mapped onto v2's page index; checked live |\n| RNAcentral | Search goes through EBI Search | `page` is mapped onto `start` |\n| ClinGen | Uses the Evidence Repository API | Paging added to it; the snapshot's summary-API path dropped |\n| DisProt | Uses gene/name filters | Every filter request is paged |\n| eQTL Catalogue, NCI cancer resources | Retired | Stay retired; the stale snapshot tests were removed |\n\nSmaller choices to look at in review:\n\n- **SAbDab: search comes back in a follow-up PR.** This PR keeps main's #701 version, in which `SAbDab_search_structures` does not search. Checked live on 2026-10-23, `/api/antibody-instances` does filter by antigen name: no filter gives `total` 22671, `binds_to_antigen=lysozyme` gives 123, `spike glycoprotein` gives 2008, and a made-up name gives 0. #701 tested `/api/pdb`, which ignores filters. The snapshot's search on `antibody-instances` will be restored on top of this PR.\n- **MedlinePlus** now returns full summaries plus `summary_length`, replacing the 500-character cut.\n- **MeSH:** `descriptor_id` is now checked locally against `[CDMQT]` + 6–9 digits, and a returned record whose identifier differs from the requested one is an error. The rule was checked against id.nlm.nih.gov on 2026-10-23. Each of these returns 200 and is accepted:\n  - descriptors `D009369` and `D000086382`\n  - qualifier `Q000009`\n  - term `T010724`\n  - concept `M0013994`\n  - supplementary records `C000657245`, `C014347` and `C537093`\n- **PubMed:** search still shows 5 authors plus `author_count` (main's choice). `PubMed_get_article` returns the full author list, collective names and all affiliations.\n- **DailyMed:** `DailyMed_search_drug_classes` keeps a `pagination: dailymed_page` config field that its own `run()` never reads. It can be removed together with the tests that use it, or wired in; that is left as a follow-up.\n\n## Tests\n\n- **317 new unit test files** for the contract, with all HTTP faked.\n- **Live regressions:** `tests/integration/test_silent_failure_report_live.py` is opt-in (`TOOLUNIVERSE_RUN_LIVE_SILENT_FAILURES=1`) and was not run for this PR.\n- **Unit suite:** run with `-m \"not network and not live\"`, against main's own run of the same command on the same machine:\n  - branch: 11255 passed, 30 failed, 1 collection error\n  - **no test fails on this branch that passes on main**\n  - 11 tests that fail on main pass here\n  - the remaining failures are environment-specific and fail on main too: `remote_resident` (`/proc/meminfo`), `/private/var` path aliasing, and a scipy `_spropack` import in `test_remote_roadmap_tools`\n- **Generated files:** wrappers were regenerated with `scripts/build_tools.py` for the tools whose config changed, and `_lazy_registry_static.py` with `generate_lazy_registry`.\n- **Formatting:** `ruff check` is clean on the changed files. `ruff format` was applied to new files and to files that were already formatted on main. Files main itself leaves unformatted were not reformatted, to keep the diff readable.\n\nThe pre-port snapshot is kept on `codex/fix-silent-failures-snapshot` for reference.\n",
